-- title:
--   Semilinear automorphisms extend uniquely along a constant field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K, F, K', F'$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ a $K'$-algebra, $K'$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ an $F$-algebra and $F'$ a $K$-algebra, the scalar actions being compatible along $K \to K' \to F'$ and along $K \to F \to F'$, and assume $K$ is algebraically closed of characteristic zero. Assume further: there is $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over the subfield $K(x)$ generated by $x$; there is $x' \in F'$ transcendental over $K'$ with $F'$ finite-dimensional over $K'(x')$; and the subfield of $F'$ generated over $K'$ by the image of $F$ under $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ F\ F'$ is all of $F'$. Here a semilinear automorphism of $F$ over $K$ (`SemilinearAut K F`) is a pair consisting of a ring automorphism of $F$ and a ring automorphism of $K$ such that the first, applied to the image of $a \in K$ in $F$, is the image of the value of the second at $a$; `baseAut` picks out the second component, and the action $g \bullet y$ is that of the first component on $F$. Given such a $g$ and a ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K'$ satisfying $\tau(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ K\ K'\ a) = \mathrm{algebraMap}\ K\ K'\ (\mathrm{baseAut}\ g\ a)$ for all $a \in K$, the conclusion is that there is exactly one semilinear automorphism $g'$ of $F'$ over $K'$ whose base automorphism equals $\tau$ at every $c \in K'$ and which satisfies $g' \bullet \mathrm{algebraMap}\ F\ F'\ y = \mathrm{algebraMap}\ F\ F'\ (g \bullet y)$ for all $y \in F$.
--
--   This is the extension of a semilinear automorphism of a one-variable function field $F/K$ to the constant field extension $F' = F \cdot K'$, compatibly with a prescribed automorphism $\tau$ of the new constant field; the hypotheses on $F$ and $F'$ say exactly that each is finite over a rational subfield, i.e. a function field in one variable. It rests on the linear disjointness statement [`AlgebraicCurve.linearIndependent_of_constantFieldExtension`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.linearIndependent_of_constantFieldExtension), and feeds the variant [`AlgebraicCurve.SemilinearAut.existsUnique_monoidHom_baseAut_eq_smul_algebraMap_eq_of_constantFieldExtension`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.SemilinearAut.existsUnique_monoidHom_baseAut_eq_smul_algebraMap_eq_of_constantFieldExtension), which assembles these extensions into a homomorphism of automorphism groups.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_SemilinearAut_existsUnique_baseAut_eq_smul_algebraMap_eq_of_constantFieldExtension.lean

